.TH QUADRF-HOTSPOT 8 "August 2026" "QuadRF" "QuadRF"
.SH NAME
quadrf-hotspot \- client, hotspot, or off for QuadRF wlan0
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B quadrf-hotspot
.RB [ start | sta | ap | off ]
.br
.B quadrf-hotspot fallback
.RB yes | no
.SH DESCRIPTION
Selects the wlan0 role. Hotspot and client cannot run together on the Pi radio.
.PP
.B start
is used at boot by
.BR quadrf-hotspot.service .
It honours
.B QUADRF_WIFI_MODE
from
.IR /etc/quadrf/quadrf.conf :
.TP
.B sta
(the default when unset) Try a saved
.B wpa_supplicant
network for twelve seconds. On success, stay in client mode. On failure,
start the hotspot only if
.B QUADRF_WIFI_FALLBACK
is yes (the default). Fallback does not change
.BR QUADRF_WIFI_MODE ,
so the next boot still retries client first.
.TP
.B ap
Start the hotspot immediately (no client wait).
.TP
.B off
Stop hostapd and wpa_supplicant and leave wlan0 down. Persists across reboot.
.PP
.BR sta , ap ,
and
.B off
are live switches from the control panel. They write
.B QUADRF_WIFI_MODE
then apply that role without a reboot.
.B fallback
only writes
.BR QUADRF_WIFI_FALLBACK .
.PP
Leaving AP mode does a link down/up: the onboard firmware needs that when
hostapd releases wlan0. Ethernet and USB paths are not affected.
.PP
.B quadrf-mdns-alias
publishes
.B quadrf.local
on each interface's own address. A LAN client sees the ethernet address, not
the access point. avahi-daemon does not publish unscoped host A records.
.PP
If client does not associate, the appliance comes up on
.B QUADRF_AP_SSID
at
.B QUADRF_AP_ADDRESS
when fallback is enabled. AP clients get a captive DNS listener that
answers every name with
.B QUADRF_AP_ADDRESS
so the phone Sign In sheet can load. That listener is bound to wlan0 via
nftables/iptables redirect; it is not
.RB address=/#/
in the shared dnsmasq, which would hijack names on eth0 and usb0.
DHCP option 114 advertises
.BR http://HOSTNAME.local/
as the portal URI. Unknown HTTP hosts serve a page naming that address;
Android and Windows probes 302 there.
.PP
The script exits with an error if
.B dtoverlay=disable-wifi
is present in the firmware configuration, since wlan0 will not exist.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/quadrf/quadrf.conf
.BR QUADRF_WIFI_MODE ,
.BR QUADRF_WIFI_FALLBACK ,
AP SSID and address.
.TP
.I /etc/wpa_supplicant/wpa_supplicant.conf
Saved client network, written by
.BR quadrf-apply-wifi (8).
.TP
.I /etc/dnsmasq.d/quadrf-wlan0-ap.conf
Names while the access point is up.
.TP
.I /etc/hostapd/quadrf.conf
Generated from
.B QUADRF_AP_SSID
by
.BR "quadrf apply" .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR quadrf (1),
.BR quadrf.conf (5),
.BR quadrf-apply-wifi (8),
.BR quadrf-apply-ap (8),
.BR quadrf-dns-update (8),
.BR quadrf-ethernet (8),
.BR quadrf-usb (8)
